92
00:06:24,429 --> 00:06:25,089
[SPEAKER_05]: It's fine.

93
00:06:25,729 --> 00:06:33,652
[SPEAKER_02]: Dear Jeffrey Driscoll and the Medford Housing Authority Board of Commissioners, hello, we are tenants of the Medford Housing Authority Phillip Building located at 15 Canal Street.

94
00:06:34,152 --> 00:06:40,276
[SPEAKER_02]: We are writing to respectfully ask that you please not remove the storage spaces in the basement permanently.

95
00:06:40,836 --> 00:06:46,520
[SPEAKER_02]: Although not everyone who lives in a building uses the storage space, for those who do, it is essential.

96
00:06:47,220 --> 00:07:01,209
[SPEAKER_02]: We use the storage spaces for ordinary things that we wish to keep, but which do not fit into our apartments, such as air conditioners, beach chairs, and Christmas decorations.

97
00:07:02,069 --> 00:07:13,146
[SPEAKER_02]: For many people, this building is a stop on the road to other places, such as Section 8, moving in with family or getting a job and moving out of public housing completely.

98
00:07:15,497 --> 00:07:25,161
[SPEAKER_02]: There are things which may fit into other parts of our lives that do not fit into our current lives, and we would like to save them.

99
00:07:25,741 --> 00:07:39,267
[SPEAKER_02]: Because everyone here has a low income, however, we are not able to afford a conventional storage unit, nor is it feasible when our storage needs are adequately served by the small space in the basement.

100
00:07:39,988 --> 00:07:40,728
[SPEAKER_02]: We are asking

101
00:07:42,038 --> 00:07:47,681
[SPEAKER_02]: that you please reconsider cutting off our access to storage space in the basement.

102
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:51,223
[SPEAKER_02]: Even a smaller space will be better than nothing.

103
00:07:52,023 --> 00:07:56,426
[SPEAKER_02]: The current space are kept clean, and I have never seen vermin there.

104
00:07:57,646 --> 00:08:02,229
[SPEAKER_02]: They are easily accessible when we want to do things like put up our Christmas tree.

105
00:08:03,109 --> 00:08:07,652
[SPEAKER_02]: They are very small things, but they have a great value to numerous people

106
00:08:08,672 --> 00:08:14,333
[SPEAKER_02]: and you will be doing a wonderful good deed by continuing allowing us to access some storage.

107
00:08:14,953 --> 00:08:17,414
[SPEAKER_02]: Thank you very much for your time and attention.

108
00:08:18,374 --> 00:08:36,238
[SPEAKER_02]: And it is signed by Kate Ryan, Beth Onafiri, I think I'm saying that right, Amy Walsh, Daniel Scarfield,

109
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:41,391
[SPEAKER_02]: Mr. Lieberman, apartment 15, and someone else.

